 "brief": "Forearm for a small robot arm, PETG on my FDM printer, printed lying flat so the layers stack\nalong Z. The elbow end has an 8 mm steel shaft running through it along Z at the origin (make\nthe hole 8.2 mm, with at least 3 mm of wall). At the wrist end the wrist servo bolts onto a flat\npad: the pad occupies x = 110 to 115, y = -12 to 12, z = -6 to 6, and it has two M3 clearance\nholes along X at y = +8 and y = -8 (z = 0). The whole part has to fit in x = -12 to 115,\ny = -15 to 15, z = -8 to 8. The wrist and gripper weigh 600 g and swing around. The shaft\nholds the forearm. It must not sag more than 0.5 mm at the wrist and needs a safety factor of 2.",
